# Template for .bazelrc.user -- network-specific Bazel settings.
#
# Copy to <repo>/.bazelrc.user (ignored by git) and keep only the blocks
# your network needs. The repository's .bazelrc imports that file if it
# exists; without it Bazel uses the public Bazel Central Registry and no
# remote cache.
#
# Never put credentials here: Bazel reads HTTP auth from ~/.netrc
#
#   machine <registry-host>
#     login <user>
#     password <api-token>

# --- Module registry mirror --------------------------------------------
# When the public Bazel Central Registry is not reachable.
# common --registry=https://<registry-host>/<path-to-bazel-modules>

# --- HTTP proxy ----------------------------------------------------------
# Bazel's registry fetches run on the JVM's HTTP client, which reads system
# properties, NOT http_proxy / https_proxy. Without these a proxy-only
# network shows a misleading "Unknown host" error.
# startup --host_jvm_args=-Dhttps.proxyHost=<proxy-host>
# startup --host_jvm_args=-Dhttps.proxyPort=<proxy-port>
# startup --host_jvm_args=-Dhttp.proxyHost=<proxy-host>
# startup --host_jvm_args=-Dhttp.proxyPort=<proxy-port>
# startup --host_jvm_args=-Dhttp.nonProxyHosts=localhost|127.0.0.1

# --- Private CA ----------------------------------------------------------
# When the registry or cache uses certificates of a private CA: a Java
# truststore holding that CA chain (keep it out of the repository).
# startup --host_jvm_args=-Djavax.net.ssl.trustStore=<path-to-truststore.jks>
# startup --host_jvm_args=-Djavax.net.ssl.trustStorePassword=<password>

# --- Remote cache --------------------------------------------------------
# build --remote_cache=https://<cache-host>/<path>/cas
# build --remote_timeout=10s
# build --remote_max_connections=100
# build --remote_accept_cached=true
# build --remote_local_fallback
# build --remote_retries=5
# Developers read only; CI is the sole writer.
# build --remote_upload_local_results=false
